Backport of feschber/lan-mouse#528 (open, head fb0e2b95fc1b) onto 0.11.0,
minus its regression-test module (the tests need macos_modifier_tests.rs and
real-time sleeps, neither of which belongs in the nix build's checkPhase).

0.11.0's macOS emulation runs every key, modifiers included, through one
repeat task and releases the repeating key whenever the next key goes down:
holding Cmd (or F18, the hyper key) and pressing A posts Cmd-up before A, and
every modifier press posts a phantom keycode-0 ("A") FlagsChanged event.
#528 gives modifiers their own FlagsChanged events and releases each key only
on its own key-up.

